    "summary": "Age-resolved alpha-knee from an APOGEE (DR18) 3-table join of 330,028 giants (apogeeDistMass C/N ages + distances, apogeeStar Galactic coordinates, aspcapStar [Fe/H]-[MG/Fe]). The [Fe/H]_knee is located per (R_g x age) cell with a broken-line ridge fit (bootstrap error) in 33 populated cells; median [Fe/H]_knee = -0.49. Gradients: d[Fe/H]_knee/d(age)|_R_g = -0.0022+/-0.0107 dex/Gyr; d[Fe/H]_knee/dR_g|_age = +0.0146+/-0.0086 dex/kpc. Non-circularity: the age-gradient sign does NOT hold under the abundance-scale swap ([Fe/H]->[M/H], [MG/Fe]->[alpha/M]).",
    "title": "Mapping the Galactic alpha-knee across stellar age and galactocentric radius",
    "provenance": "Real SDSS DR18 APOGEE catalog data via SkyServer raw-HTTP (no astroquery). Three tables (apogeeDistMass, apogeeStar, aspcapStar) are pulled as bare columns, chunked by sky region with pacing + retry/backoff + disk cache, and joined in-process on APOGEE_ID; flag/quality cuts (STAR_BAD, per-element flags, SNR, abundance errors, 1-14 Gyr ages) are applied in Python. R_g is computed from glon/glat/distance with R0=8.122 kpc. Ages are spectroscopic C/N (data-driven) and carry the known C/N-age systematics; the alpha-knee and its gradients are the reported quantities, and the non-circularity test swaps the abundance calibration scale, not the data set.",
    "figure_url": "/api/lab/runs/ovl2627305/artifact/result.png"
